  "body": "Found in the second read of PR #3413 (head b38f0c12f). The label `bug` applies.\n\n## What happens\nA Face operation with protected items clips its rows by a keep-out. The keep-out of a level covers the heights from that level up to the clearance plane. A lower level gets the same keep-out or a larger one. Thus the blocked levels are always the lowest levels.\n\nWhen one or more levels are blocked and one level stays clear, the operation generates. The face can stop above Cut Z in each place. The only sign is the note \"blocked N facing level(s); the remaining levels stayed clear\" (`crates/motion/src/machining2d/face_keep.rs:425-429`).\n\nThe note does not say that Cut Z was not reached. Nothing marks the operation \"incomplete\". The Prime Directive says: \"If an operation can only be computed in part, mark it 'incomplete'.\"\n\nThe result is not a gouge. Material stays that the user expects to be removed.\n\n## Wanted\n- When a blocked level leaves the face above Cut Z, the operation says so in plain English with the depth that it reached, and it is marked \"incomplete\" (or refused: record the decision).\n- A test with a keep-out that changes with Z (an item that is wider at a lower level) pins the message and the state.\n",
